  "result": "I've implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 12 tests to `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes all 14 tests (12 new, 2 existing).\n\n**How it works, in order:**\n1. Lowercases the text.\n2. Removes accents, so `ế` and `ñ` become `e` and `n`.\n3. Maps Latin letters that don't lose their marks that way to plain letters: `đ`/`Đ` becomes `d`. I also added `ø`, `ł`, `ß`, `æ`, `œ`, `ð`, `þ` and `ı`, which you didn't ask for. Without them, a word like \"Straße\" would be split by a hyphen instead of becoming \"strasse\".\n4. Turns every run of characters that aren't `a-z` or `0-9` into a single hyphen, then removes hyphens at the start and end.\n5. Cuts the slug to 50 characters, then removes any hyphen left at the end by the cut.\n\n**The tests cover:**\n- Vietnamese text and `đ`/`Đ`\n- French, Spanish, Danish, German and Polish letters\n- collapsing runs of separators into one hyphen\n- trimming leading and trailing hyphens\n- digits\n- input with no letters or digits, which gives an empty string\n- the 50-character limit, including a cut that lands on a hyphen and a slug of exactly 50 characters that is left whole\n\nInput with no letters or digits returns an empty string; if you'd rather it threw an error or returned a fallback, say so.",
